    "profile_text": {
        "body": "The material held here is thin and partly inconsistent. The record lists RICHTECH ROBOTICS INC. as a public company headquartered in Las Vegas, Nevada, with the ticker RR and the website rolls-royce.com, and the text drawn from that site describes Rolls-Royce rather than Richtech Robotics. According to that site, Rolls-Royce develops and delivers complex power and propulsion solutions for safety-critical applications in the air, at sea and on land, and describes itself as having been at the forefront of innovation for more than 100 years. The site also cites a £300 million investment in UK manufacturing and engineering facilities, a completed $1 billion investment in Indiana, a stated intent with Reliance Industries to partner on India's indigenous combat engine for the Advanced Medium Combat Aircraft (AMCA) programme, and planned co-operation with the United Kingdom National Nuclear Laboratory and the Japan Atomic Energy Agency on advanced nuclear technologies.\n\nThe held facts add little beyond the corporate record. No AI products are tracked, no MCP servers are listed, and no lawsuits are recorded. The company is registered in Nevada, where the count of recorded cases is zero. A CIK, 0001963685, is on file.",
